### 171: PASS With Explicit Boundary-Only Ambiguity, ungraded appropriate

The unique line is y=x/5, through (0,0),(5,1). The upper side is uniquely
determined: the component strictly above this line is y>x/5; its closure is
y>=x/5. Neither is the unrelated coordinate half-plane y>0.

If "half-plane determined by a line" means a component of the plane with the
line removed, the intended inequality is y>x/5. If "half-plane" includes its
defining boundary, the intended inequality is y>=x/5. The authorized statement
does not specify that convention or supply a definition. Adjacent non-strict
exercises and the TEXT_PASS receipt do not logically settle it.

The exact limited ambiguity is membership of points (t,t/5), t real, only.
All strictly above and all strictly below points have unambiguous membership.
The candidate concretely identifies both sets, labels the closed alternative,
and does not conflate them as auto-gradable answers. Its requested line and
upper-side answers are mathematically complete under the stated limitation.
No content revision is required for this scoped mathematical review.
No human or other review has been claimed to confirm either boundary convention.
The author's note requesting convention confirmation is not evidence of such
confirmation, nor an authorization for another stage.

